There's a bug in my code: `board.querySelector(".card") && board.querySelector(".card").focus()` — this is awkward and could throw if there's no card. Let me simplify it. Also, `event.target.closest` — if event.target is a text node or the target isn't an Element, `.closest` won't exist. But click targets are elements. However, `event.target` could be a text node in some cases... actually no, click event targets are always elements.

Let me fix the restart focus line to be cleaner.

Also I should double check: `firstCard = null` after computing `a` and `b`. In `onMatch`, I reference `firstCard` but I already set it to null before calling `onMatch(b, gem)`. Let me check:

```js
var a = firstCard;
var b = card;
firstCard = null;

if (a.dataset.gem === b.dataset.gem) {
  onMatch(b, gem);
}
```

In `onMatch`, I do:
```js
function onMatch(card, gem) {
  card.classList.add("is-matched");
  ...
  if (firstCard) {  // firstCard is null here!
    firstCard.classList.add("is-matched");
    ...
  }
```

That's a bug — `firstCard` is already null, so card `a` never gets `is-matched`. Let me fix `onMatch` to take both cards.

Let me rewrite that function properly.

